# .trivyignore — review-approved exceptions for the trivy image CVE gate.
#
# Policy (AUT-1749): the base-image scan (.github/workflows/trivy-image-scan.yml)
# fails on HIGH/CRITICAL CVEs that have an upstream fix. Only CVEs listed here are
# tolerated, and each MUST carry a justification + the PR/issue that approved it.
# Prefer a digest bump over an ignore entry whenever a fixed image exists.
#
# Format: one CVE id per line (leading `#` = comment; empty lines ignored).
#
# Example (do NOT ship blind suppressions — only add a CVE after confirming it is
# not exploitable in our usage and the CTO/security reviewer has signed off):
# CVE-2024-0000  # accepted: bookworm-slim base, no network-exposed listener; review AUT-XXXX

# --- AUT-1749: pgvector/pgvector:pg17 gosu-stdlib CVEs -----------------------
# Source: the `gosu` binary (GOSU_VERSION=1.19) bundled in the postgres image.
# trivy attributes Go stdlib CVEs to it (package "stdlib", Go 1.24/1.25). gosu
# is used ONLY to drop privileges before exec'ing postgres — it performs no
# network/TLS/URL/XML/MIME/HTTP2 processing, so none of these are reachable in
# AutoBrain's Postgres data-store role. Confirmed: the pinned pg17 digest has
# ZERO postgres/debian HIGH|CRITICAL CVEs; all 22 findings are gosu-stdlib.
# Flagged for security-reviewer acknowledgement on PR #306 (AUT-1749).
CVE-2025-61726  # gosu-stdlib: net/url; unreachable in privilege-drop helper
CVE-2025-61729  # gosu-stdlib: net/url; unreachable
CVE-2025-68121  # gosu-stdlib: crypto/tls cert validation; gosu does no TLS
CVE-2026-25679  # gosu-stdlib; unreachable in privilege-drop helper
CVE-2026-27145  # gosu-stdlib; unreachable
CVE-2026-32280  # gosu-stdlib; unreachable
CVE-2026-32281  # gosu-stdlib; unreachable
CVE-2026-32283  # gosu-stdlib; unreachable
CVE-2026-33811  # gosu-stdlib; unreachable
CVE-2026-33814  # gosu-stdlib; unreachable
CVE-2026-33818  # gosu-stdlib; unreachable
CVE-2026-39820  # gosu-stdlib; unreachable
CVE-2026-39821  # gosu-stdlib: idna/punycode; gosu does no DNS
CVE-2026-39822  # gosu-stdlib: os.Root symlink; gosu exec's a fixed target
CVE-2026-39836  # gosu-stdlib: net NUL byte; unreachable
CVE-2026-42499  # gosu-stdlib: net/mail; gosu parses no mail
CVE-2026-42504  # gosu-stdlib: mime; unreachable
CVE-2026-56853  # gosu-stdlib: net/http HTTP/2; gosu does no HTTP
CVE-2026-56858  # gosu-stdlib: html/template; unreachable
CVE-2026-56859  # gosu-stdlib: encoding/xml; unreachable
CVE-2026-56860  # gosu-stdlib: net/url; unreachable
CVE-2026-56862  # gosu-stdlib: crypto/tls KeyUpdate; gosu does no TLS

# --- AUT-1735 / python base image HIGH CVEs (unused at runtime) ------------------
# Both findings are pre-installed pip packages shipped in the python:3.13-slim
# base image (PYTHON_BASE_IMAGE). grep across the repo confirms NEITHER msgpack
# nor setuptools is imported or invoked by any AutoBrain runtime service
# (backend/ai/worker/market-data), so neither is reachable.
# python:3.13-slim@sha256:7ce4b6d... is the LATEST 3.13-slim digest (Docker Hub
# confirmed) — no digest bump carries patched wheels — so suppress per policy
# ("tolerate when no fixed image exists") until a 3.13-slim respin ships them.
# Time-boxed: re-check 2026-11-28; drop entries + bump PYTHON_BASE_IMAGE digest
# once a 3.13-slim ships msgpack>=1.2.1 and setuptools>=78.1.1.
# Security Officer sign-off requested — see child issue AUT-1844 (sign-off).
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964  # msgpack OOB read: not imported by any runtime service
CVE-2025-47273  # setuptools PackageIndex path traversal: build-time only, no runtime install path

# --- nginx:stable-alpine libexpat CVEs (time-boxed) ----------------------------
# Source: libexpat 2.8.3-r0 bundled in nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged:stable-alpine
# (alpine 3.24.1). Fixed upstream in libexpat 2.8.4-r0; no alpine rebuild has
# landed yet (2026-09-02). CVE-2026-66046 and CVE-2026-76641 are both DoS-class
# (denial of service via crafted XML) — nginx's default build does NOT compile
# the XML module (ngx_http_xml_module) and none of the AutoBrain reverse-proxy
# configs load it, so the vulnerability is not reachable.
# Time-boxed: re-check 2026-10-02; drop entries once a new stable-alpine tag
# ships libexpat >= 2.8.4-r0.
# Security Officer sign-off requested — see child issue AUT-2126.
CVE-2026-66046  # libexpat DoS: XML parsing unreachable — nginx XML module not compiled
CVE-2026-76641  # libexpat DoS: XML parsing unreachable — nginx XML module not compiled

# --- python:3.13-slim openssl QUIC DoS (CVE-2026-14456, AUT-1740) ---------------
# Source: openssl 3.5.6-1~deb13u2 (libssl3t64 / openssl / openssl-provider-legacy)
# bundled in python:3.13-slim@sha256:7ce4b6d... (debian 13.6). Fixed upstream in
# 3.5.7-1~deb13u2; no python:3.13-slim respin has shipped the patched openssl
# yet (2026-09-02). The vulnerability is unbounded memory growth in the OpenSSL
# QUIC SERVER. AutoBrain python services (backend/ai/worker/market-data) do not
# run a QUIC listener — FastAPI/uvicorn serve HTTP only, no QUIC negotiation is
# attempted at any ingress. Confirmed by grep across backend/ai/worker code:
# no `quic`, `nghttp3`, or `msquic` imports anywhere in the runtime services.
# Tracked in AUT-1844 (existing python ignore time-box); re-check 2026-11-28
# alongside the msgpack/setuptools entries. Drop + bump PYTHON_BASE_IMAGE
# digest once a python:3.13-slim ships openssl >= 3.5.7-1~deb13u2.
CVE-2026-14456  # openssl QUIC server DoS: not reachable — no QUIC listener in python runtime
